<title>GERMANY: Krupp, Thyssen shares suspended.</title>
<headline>Krupp, Thyssen shares suspended.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German industrial groups Fried. Krupp AG Hoesch-Krupp and Thyssen AG were suspended from trade on German bourses on Tuesday pending announcements from both companies, the Frankfurt stock exchange said.</p>
<p>Thyssen said in a statement late on Monday that Krupp planned a hostile takeover and that it would use &quot;all appropriate measures&quot; to ward off any grab for control by its rival.</p>
<p>Thyssen has called a news conference for Tuesday afternoon. Krupp on Monday night declined comment but said it would issue a press release.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
